#@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
#@type = "customer.portal"

Feature: DXP Release Notes
	Testing the DXP Release Notes portlet

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I log into the support homepage as "${staticSupportAdminEmailAdress}" with password "${staticSupportAdminPassword}"
	* I go to the DXP Release Notes page

Scenario: Refine Changelog Multiple Page Search Results
	Changelog search refining on multiple pages should work properly

	Given I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.0" product from "Fix Pack 71" to "Fix Pack 76"
	And I go to the Changelog tab
	And I refine the current search using the following refinement criteria
	| Application Security | true |
	Then the results count should say that there are "9" results
	And the changelog entry with the content "Multiple LDAP System Settings entries" should be visible with the following values
	| Summary   | Multiple LDAP System Settings entries                               |
	| Component | Application Security > LDAP, Portal Configuration > System Settings |
	| Release   | Fix Pack 76                                                         |
	| Key       | LPS-88275                                                           |
	And the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Google Guava" should be visible with the following values
	| Summary   | Security vulnerabilities in Google Guava |
	| Component | Application Security > Google Login      |
	| Release   | Fix Pack 73                              |
	| Key       | LPE-16664                                |
	And the changelog entry with the content "Empty Attributes in LDAP request can cause it to be rejected" should be visible with the following values
	| Summary   | Empty Attributes in LDAP request can cause it to be rejected |
	| Component | Application Security > LDAP	                          	   |
	| Release   | Fix Pack 73                                                  |
	| Key       | LPS-89295                                                    |
	And the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Google Guava" should be visible with the following values
	| Summary   | Security vulnerabilities in Google Guava |
	| Component | Application Security > Google Login      |
	| Release   | Fix Pack 73	                           |
	| Key       | LPE-16664                                |
	When I clear all search refinements
	Then the results count should say that there are "129" results
	When I refine the current search using the following refinement criteria
	| Contains Text | Security Vulnerabilities |
	Then the results count should say that there are "8" results
	And the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Apache PDFBox" should be visible with the following values
	| Summary   | Security vulnerabilities in Apache PDFBox |
	| Component | DM, Security Vulnerability	            |
	| Release   | Fix Pack 75                               |
	| Key       | LPE-16681                                 |
	And the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Apache Batik" should be visible with the following values
	| Summary   | Security vulnerabilities in Apache Batik                |
	| Component | Application Security > AntiSamy, Security Vulnerability |
	| Release   | Fix Pack 75                                             |
	| Key       | LPE-16680                                               |
	And the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Spring core" should be visible with the following values
	| Summary   | Security vulnerabilities in Spring core     |
	| Component | Core Infrastructure, Security Vulnerability |
	| Release   | Fix Pack 75                                 |
	| Key       | LPE-16659                                   |
	And the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Netty" should be visible with the following values
	| Summary   | Security vulnerabilities in Netty           |
	| Component | Core Infrastructure, Security Vulnerability |
	| Release   | Fix Pack 73                                 |
	| Key       | LPE-16660                                   |
	And the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Apache Tika" should be visible with the following values
	| Summary   | Security vulnerabilities in Apache Tika |
	| Component | DM, Security Vulnerability              |
	| Release   | Fix Pack 72                             |
	| Key       | LPE-16653                               |
	When I clear all search refinements
	Then the results count should say that there are "129" results
	When I refine the current search using the following refinement criteria
	| Contains Text          | Apache PDFBox |
	| Document Management    | true          |
	| Security Vulnerability | true          |
	Then the results count should say that there are "1" results
	And the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Apache PDFBox" should be visible with the following values
	| Summary   | Security vulnerabilities in Apache PDFBox |
	| Component | DM, Security Vulnerability	            |
	| Release   | Fix Pack 75                               |
	| Key       | LPE-16681                                 |
	When I clear all search refinements
	Then the results count should say that there are "129" results
	And the current page number of the results page should be page "1"
	And the changelog entry with the content "Error Message after the session expires is not translated" should be visible with the following values
	| Summary   | Error Message after the session expires is not translated |
	| Component | Portal Services, Portal Services > Localization           |
	| Release   | Fix Pack 76                                               |
	| Key       | LPS-86172                                                 |
	And the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Spring core" should be visible with the following values
	| Summary   | Security vulnerabilities in Spring core     |
	| Component | Core Infrastructure, Security Vulnerability |
	| Release   | Fix Pack 75                                 |
	| Key       | LPE-16659                                   |
	When I go to the next page of the search results
	Then the current page number of the results page should be page "2"
	And the changelog entry with the content "JS error when selecting pagination limit" should be visible with the following values
	| Summary   | JS error when selecting pagination limit |
	| Component | ~ [Archived] Frontend Infrastructure	   |
	| Release   | Fix Pack 73                              |
	| Key       | LPS-89876                                |
	And the changelog entry with the content "Same scheduler job may be executed in two threads at the same time" should be visible with the following values
	| Summary   | Same scheduler job may be executed in two threads at the same time |
	| Component | Portal Services > Scheduler	                  	                 |
	| Release   | Fix Pack 73                                                        |
	| Key       | LPS-89033                                                          |
	When I go to the next page of the search results
	Then the current page number of the results page should be page "3"
	And the changelog entry with the content "Metadata value is missing after uploading multiple documents" should be visible with the following values
	| Summary   | Metadata value is missing after uploading multiple documents |
	| Component | Dynamic Data Mapping	                                       |
	| Release   | Fix Pack 71                                                  |
	| Key       | LPS-83714                                                    |
	And the changelog entry with the content "StagedAuditedModel is not found when using service builder" should be visible with the following values
	| Summary   | StagedAuditedModel is not found when using service builder |
	| Component | Core Infrastructure > Service Builder	        	         |
	| Release   | Fix Pack 71                                                |
	| Key       | LPS-89567                                                  |

