Scenario: Sort Changelog Multiple Page Search Results
	Changelog search sorting on multiple pages should work properly

	Given I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.0" product from "Fix Pack 71" to "Fix Pack 76"
	And I go to the Changelog tab
	Then the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 76" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 75" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 74" should be visible
	When I go to the next page of the search results
	Then the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 74" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 73" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 72" should be visible
	When I go to the next page of the search results
	Then the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 72" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 71" should be visible
	When I sort the changelog results in ascending order
	Then the current page number of the results page should be page "1"
	Then the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 71" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 72" should be visible
	When I go to the next page of the search results
	Then the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 72" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 73" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 74" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 75" should be visible
	When I go to the next page of the search results
	Then the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 75" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 76" should be visible
	When I go to the previous page of the search results
	And I sort the changelog results in descending order
	Then the current page number of the results page should be page "1"
	Then the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 76" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 75" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 74" should be visible
	When I go to the next page of the search results
	Then the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 74" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 73" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 72" should be visible
	When I go to the next page of the search results
	Then the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 72" should be visible
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 71" should be visible

Scenario: Sort Changelog Refined Search Results
	Changelog search sorting on refined results should work properly

	Given I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.0" product from "Fix Pack 71" to "Fix Pack 76"
	And I go to the Changelog tab
	And I refine the current search using the following refinement criteria
	| Application Security | true |
	Then the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 76" should be in position number "1"
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 75" should be in position number "4"
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 73" should be in position number "6"
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 72" should be in position number "8"
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 71" should be in position number "9"
	When I sort the changelog results in ascending order
	Then the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 71" should be in position number "1"
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 72" should be in position number "2"
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 73" should be in position number "5"
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 75" should be in position number "7"
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 76" should be in position number "9"
	When I sort the changelog results in descending order
	Then the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 76" should be in position number "1"
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 75" should be in position number "4"
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 73" should be in position number "6"
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 72" should be in position number "8"
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 71" should be in position number "9"
	When I clear all search refinements
	And I refine the current search using the following refinement criteria
	| Contains Text | Security Vulnerabilities |
	Then the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 75" should be in position number "1"
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 73" should be in position number "6"
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 72" should be in position number "8"
	When I sort the changelog results in ascending order
	Then the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 72" should be in position number "1"
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 73" should be in position number "2"
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 75" should be in position number "4"
	When I sort the changelog results in descending order
	Then the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 75" should be in position number "1"
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 73" should be in position number "6"
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 72" should be in position number "8"

Scenario: Sort Changelog Single Page Search Results
	Changelog search sorting on a single page should work properly

	Given I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.0" product from "Fix Pack 75" to "Fix Pack 76"
	And I go to the Changelog tab
	Then the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 76" should be in position number "1"
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 75" should be in position number "43"
	When I sort the changelog results in ascending order
	Then the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 75" should be in position number "1"
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 76" should be in position number "43"
	When I sort the changelog results in descending order
	Then the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 76" should be in position number "1"
	And the changelog entry with the version "Fix Pack 75" should be in position number "43"

Scenario: View Changelog Multiple Page Search Result Details
	Changelog search details on multiple pages should work properly

	Given I set the search filters to the "DXP 7.0" product from "Fix Pack 71" to "Fix Pack 76"
	And I go to the Changelog tab
	And I click on the changelog entry with the content "Error Message after the session expires is not translated"
	Then the changelog entry details with the content "Error Message after the session expires is not translated" should be visible
	When I close the changelog details window
	And I click on the changelog entry with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Spring core"
	Then the changelog entry details with the content "Security vulnerabilities in Spring core" should be visible
	When I close the changelog details window
	And I go to the next page of the search results
	And I click on the changelog entry with the content "JS error when selecting pagination limit"
	Then the changelog entry details with the content "JS error when selecting pagination limit" should be visible
	When I close the changelog details window
	And I click on the changelog entry with the content "Same scheduler job may be executed in two threads at the same time"
	Then the changelog entry details with the content "Same scheduler job may be executed in two threads at the same time" should be visible
	When I close the changelog details window
	And I go to the next page of the search results
	And I click on the changelog entry with the content "Metadata value is missing after uploading multiple documents"
	Then the changelog entry details with the content "Metadata value is missing after uploading multiple documents" should be visible
	When I close the changelog details window
	And I click on the changelog entry with the content "StagedAuditedModel is not found when using service builder"
	Then the changelog entry details with the content "StagedAuditedModel is not found when using service builder" should be visible

